WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.060
If you think that much of anything related
to politics will be settled by Tuesday's election,

00:00:05.060 --> 00:00:08.840
here's some bad news for you: Nothing that
matters is really over.

00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:10.660
"Nothing is over!

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:11.260
Nothing!"

00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:13.960
There are at least three major issues facing
the country

00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:18.560
when either President Clinton or President Trump gets sworn in next January.

00:00:23.310 --> 00:00:27.519
You may not realize it, but the U.S. has been
out of recession for seven years.

00:00:27.519 --> 00:00:31.699
But the average rate of growth since 2009
has been around 2 percent,

00:00:31.700 --> 00:00:35.620
making this the weakest economic recovery since 1949.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:38.760
Economic growth is essential to improving
living standards,

00:00:38.760 --> 00:00:42.300
and it helps to defuse all sorts of explosive political issues,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:44.800
from trade to immigration to welfare.

00:00:44.800 --> 00:00:49.780
But for all of the 21st century economic growth
has been much lower than what we're used to.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:54.080
Neither Clinton or Trump has put forth a plan
that will actually grow the economy.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:56.680
Clinton will jack up taxes and spending on
everything,

00:00:56.680 --> 00:00:59.840
a sure-fire way to keep the economy sputtering along.

00:00:59.840 --> 00:01:03.200
Trump will add more than five-trillion dollars
to the national debt,

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:05.100
which will also dampen growth.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.960
Hillary Clinton is a hawk's hawk who has voted
for, lobbied for, or taken credit for

00:01:13.960 --> 00:01:17.500
all of our military interventions in the 21st
century.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:23.860
Despite such actions—or more accurately,
BECAUSE of such actions—the world is a mess.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:26.780
At times Donald Trump sounds like he would
be a relative dove

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:29.660
and at others, he sounds like a crazy man;

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:34.720
at the very least, like Hillary Clinton, he said that he would increase military spending.

00:01:34.720 --> 00:01:37.420
Neither of them has articulated a foreign
policy

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:39.500
that will help reduce international terrorism,

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:43.340
or bring order and peace to hot
spots in the Middle East, Eastern Europe,

00:01:43.350 --> 00:01:45.010
or Asia any time soon.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.760
Trust and confidence in most American institutions
are at or near historic lows

00:01:53.760 --> 00:01:57.960
—the media, religious organizations, labor, business—you name it.

00:01:57.970 --> 00:02:01.350
That's especially true when it comes to the
two major political parties

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:02.790
and government in general.

00:02:02.790 --> 00:02:07.700
Even worse, millennials aren't just the biggest
generation, they are the most skeptical.

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:09.880
Who can blame them—or us?

00:02:09.890 --> 00:02:13.570
The Iraq War was sold on bad information and
prosecuted poorly;

00:02:13.570 --> 00:02:17.040
President Obama's claims that his health care reform would let you keep your doctor

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:19.940
was the Lie of the Year in 2013,

00:02:19.940 --> 00:02:23.120
and we've learned that Democrats and
Republicans don't give a rat's ass

00:02:23.120 --> 00:02:25.200
about the government spying on us.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.720
Wikileaks and others have exposed Hillary
Clinton as two-faced at best

00:02:28.720 --> 00:02:31.880
and Donald Trump is a serial scam artist and bully.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:35.920
Neither will address the massive and ongoing
evacuation of trust and confidence

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:37.560
in government and politics.

00:02:37.560 --> 00:02:41.080
If anything, they will likely pour gas on
this dumpster fire.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:45.440
This means America is moving rapidly from a high-trust society to a low-trust one

00:02:45.440 --> 00:02:47.380
and that's really bad news,

00:02:47.380 --> 00:02:51.740
especially for those of us who want
a government that spends less and does less.

00:02:51.740 --> 00:02:53.760
Why? because paradoxically,

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:57.840
people in low-trust
countries turn to government in ever-higher numbers.

00:02:57.840 --> 00:03:03.240
In a cruel and unpredictable world, they want
a protector, no matter how untrustworthy.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.900
Politicians and their supporters can act responsibly

00:03:05.900 --> 00:03:10.540
and put forth serious plans for reducing the size, scope and spending of government.

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:13.410
Gary Johnson and Bill Weld did precisely this.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.270
The two former governors spoke not of zero government
but of smaller government

00:03:17.270 --> 00:03:20.090
that did fewer things more effectively.

00:03:20.090 --> 00:03:22.490
Such characters are few and far between

00:03:22.490 --> 00:03:24.780
but there are enough elected officials in each party

00:03:24.780 --> 00:03:28.879
to at least insist on government performing
its basic functions.

00:03:28.879 --> 00:03:31.450
Such as passing actual budgets each year.

00:03:31.450 --> 00:03:34.690
Until the major parties start governing in
the light of day

00:03:34.690 --> 00:03:39.360
and especially stop nominating candidates who are distrusted by majorities of Americans,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.960
don't expect much to change.

00:03:40.960 --> 00:03:43.120
Except for things to get even nastier.

